@node Project Overview
@chapter Project Overview

EIGHTBOL is a compiler for 8-bit and 16-bit microprocessor systems. It accepts
programs written in seventeen different higher-level languages and generates
efficient assembly code for a wide variety of processors.

@section Supported Languages

EIGHTBOL currently supports compilation from:
AGI, BASIC, Burgermistress, COBOL, FORTH, FORTRAN, Lingo, Lua, Muddle,
Objective-C, Pascal, SCI, SCUMM, SmallTalk, and ZIL.

@section Supported Target Processors

EIGHTBOL generates assembly code for:
6502, 65c02, 65c816, HuC6280, RP2A03, cp1610, Z80, SM83, m68k, i286,
ARM7 (Thumb), F8, and a stack-based virtual machine.

@section Project Statistics

As of September 2026:
@itemize @bullet
@item 23 error classes with 165+ error tests
@item 57/57 COBOL AST nodes implemented
@item 15+ language frontends with comprehensive coverage
@item 14 backend architectures
@item Comprehensive test suite with FiveAM integration
@end itemize

