@node Error Handling Guide
@chapter Error Handling and Restart Patterns

@section Error Class Hierarchy

EIGHTBOL uses a structured condition class hierarchy for error handling:

@itemize @bullet
@item @code{COMPILER-ERROR} --- Base class for all compiler errors
@item @code{SOURCE-ERROR} --- Parse and syntax errors
@item @code{SEMANTIC-ERROR} --- Type and semantic errors
@item @code{BACKEND-ERROR} --- Code generation failures
@item @code{COPYBOOK-ERROR} --- File inclusion issues
@item @code{VALIDATION-ERROR} --- Constraint violations
@end itemize

@section Error Reporting Best Practices

@subsection For Parser/Syntax Errors

Use @code{source-error} with full context:

@example
(error 'source-error
       :source-file (current-file)
       :source-line (current-line)
       :source-sequence (current-seq)
       :message "Unexpected token DIVIDE")
@end example

@subsection For Backend Errors

Use @code{backend-error} with processor context:

@example
(error 'backend-error
       :cpu :6502
       :message "DIVIDE not supported"
       :detail "Use bit shift or target 65C816")
@end example

@subsection For Copybook Issues

Use specific copybook error types:

@example
(error 'copybook-not-found
       :copybook-name "Classes"
       :library "Source/Classes"
       :message "Cannot find copybook")
@end example

