@node AST Reference
@chapter Abstract Syntax Tree Reference

@section AST Node Types

The EIGHTBOL AST consists of canonical plist-based nodes representing
language constructs:

@subsection Move Statement
@code{(:move :source src-expr :destination dest-expr)}

@subsection Add Statement
@code{(:add :left left-expr :right right-expr :giving result-var)}

@subsection Subtract Statement
@code{(:subtract :left left-expr :right right-expr :giving result-var)}

@subsection Compute Statement
@code{(:compute :target var-name :expression expr)}

@subsection If/Then/Else Statement
@code{(:if :condition cond-expr :then then-body :else else-body)}

@subsection Perform Statement
@code{(:perform :procedure proc-name :using using-expr)}

@subsection Invoke Statement
@code{(:invoke :object obj-ref :method "MethodName" :using using-expr)}

@subsection String Block Transfer
@code{(:string-blt :source src-var :destination dest-var :length len-expr)}

@section AST Serialization Format

AST nodes are serialized to @file{Object/Classes/ClassName.eightbol} as
S-expressions (plists). This allows round-trip serialization and
deserialization.

@section AST Optimization

The @code{:ast-optimize} test suite verifies AST transformations and
optimizations. See @file{tests/ast-optimize.lisp} for optimization rules.

@node Backend Reference
@chapter Backend Reference and Code Generation

@section Backend Architecture

Each backend is a self-contained code generator:

@itemize @bullet
@item Read serialized AST from .eightbol file
@item Perform target-specific analysis
@item Generate processor-specific assembly code
@item Write output to .s file
@end itemize

@section Supported Backends

@subsection 6502 Family
6502, 65c02, 65c816 with extensive support for indexed addressing,
bit operations, and processor-specific features.

@subsection Other 8-bit
HuC6280 (PC Engine), RP2A03 (NES), Z80, SM83 (Game Boy), cp1610 (Intellivision).

@subsection 16-bit
m68k (Motorola 68000), i286 (Intel 80286), ARM7 (Thumb).

@subsection Virtual
Stack-based virtual machine with standard instruction set.

@section Backend Error Handling

Backends report errors via @code{backend-error} condition:

@example
(error 'backend-error
       :cpu :6502
       :statement 'divide
       :message "DIVIDE not supported on this CPU")
@end example

